#: ../../../editors.rst:4
msgid "Editor and IDE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:7
msgid "Sublime Text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:8
msgid ""
"There is a `xonsh package`_ for **Sublime Text 4** (build > 4075). To "
"install:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:10
msgid ""
"Via **Package Control**: open (``^``/``⌘`` ``⇧`` ``P``) ``Command Palette`` "
"→ ``Package Control: Install Package`` → ``xonsh``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:11
msgid ""
"**Manually**: clone the repository to your `Sublime Text packages`_ "
"directory and rename it to ``xonsh``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:13
msgid ""
"cd /path/to/sublime/packages/directory\n"
"git clone https://github.com/eugenesvk/sublime-xonsh.git\n"
"mv sublime-xonsh xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:24
msgid "Visual Studio Code (VS Code)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:25
msgid ""
"There is a `xonsh extension for VS Code`_. To install search \"xonsh\" using "
"extensions menu or just press ``F1`` and run without `>` preceding:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:28
msgid "ext install jnoortheen.xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:34
msgid ""
"Since version 1.86 of VS Code, the editor also supports loading the "
"environment for users with xonsh as their default shell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:40
msgid "JetBrains: IntelliJ IDEA, PyCharm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:41
msgid ""
"There is a `xonsh-jetbrains <https://github.com/nahoj/xonsh-jetbrains>`_ "
"plugin for JetBrains products."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:44
msgid "Emacs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:47
msgid "Emacs Xonsh mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:49
msgid ""
"There is an emacs mode for editing xonsh scripts available from the `MELPA "
"repository`_. If you are not familiar see the installation instructions "
"there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:53
msgid "Then just add this line to your emacs configuration file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:55
msgid "(require 'xonsh-mode)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:64
msgid "Xonsh Comint buffer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:66
msgid ""
"You can use xonsh as your `interactive shell in Emacs <https://www.gnu.org/"
"software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Interactive-Shell.html>`_ in a Comint "
"buffer. This way you keep all the Emacs editing power in the shell, but you "
"lose xonsh's completion feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:71
msgid ""
"Make sure you install xonsh with readline support and in your :doc:`xonsh RC "
"<xonshrc>` define"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:74
msgid "$SHELL_TYPE = 'readline'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:78
msgid ""
"Also, in Emacs set ``explicit-shell-file-name`` to your xonsh executable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:81
msgid "Xonsh Ansi-term buffer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:83
msgid ""
"The second option is to run xonsh in an Ansi-term buffer inside Emacs. This "
"way you have to switch modes if you want do Emacs-style editing, but you "
"keep xonsh's impressive completion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:87
msgid ""
"For this it is preferred to have xonsh installed with the prompt-toolkit. "
"Then you can leave ``$SHELL_TYPE`` at its default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:90
msgid ""
"Emacs will prompt you for the path of the xonsh executable when you start up "
"``ansi-term``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:94
msgid "Vim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:96
msgid "There is `xonsh syntax file for vim`_. To install run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:98
msgid "git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/linkinpark342/xonsh-vim ~/.vim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:106
msgid "Formatting xonsh code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:108
msgid ""
"Xonsh ships a built-in code formatter accessible as the ``xonsh format`` "
"subcommand. It can be wired into any editor that lets you pipe the current "
"buffer through an external command — point the editor at ``xonsh format -`` "
"to read the buffer from stdin and replace it with the formatted output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../editors.rst:114
msgid ""
"See :ref:`formatting_xonsh_code` for the full set of invocations and flags."
msgstr ""
